.TH tupie n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupie
.PP
A Mermaid\-style \fBpie chart\fR renderer for the \fBtuflow\fR diagram family. It parses a Mermaid \fBpie\fR block into a small model and renders it to SVG or PNG with the pure\-Tcl drawing backends (\fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR). No Tk, no browser, no external rasteriser.
.PP
A pie chart is not a node\-edge graph, so \fBtupie\fR does \fBnot\fR go through \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR; it owns its own parse and draw step, exposing the same \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR shape \fBtudiagram\fR uses. That lets the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade treat every diagram family uniformly: \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR detect a \fBpie\fR block and dispatch here.
.PP
A slice is drawn as a filled polygon (centre plus arc\-sampled rim points), so the \fBsame\fR routine renders identically on the raster and the SVG backend.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tupie 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tupie::parse    text                          ;# -> model dict
::tclutils::tupie::toSvg     model ?-opt val ...?          ;# -> SVG string
::tclutils::tupie::toPng     model ?-opt val ...?          ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tupie::writeSvg  model file ?-opt val ...?     ;# -> file (SVG)
::tclutils::tupie::writePng  model file ?-opt val ...?     ;# -> file (PNG)
.CE
.PP
\fBparse\fR turns Mermaid \fBpie\fR source into a model dict with keys \fBtitle\fR (string, may be empty), \fBshowData\fR (\fB0\fR|\fB1\fR) and \fBslices\fR (a list of \fB{label value}\fR pairs). The render commands take that model.
.PP
Render options (all optional):
.CS
-width  N      diagram width in logical px        (default 480)
-height N      diagram height in logical px        (default 320)
-legend 0|1    show the legend column             (default 1)
-scale  N      raster scale, positive integer     (default 1; toPng only effect)
-fontfile F    real TTF/OTF for labels (raster)   (default: 6x8 bitmap font)
.CE
.PP
The SVG backend ignores \fB\-scale\fR and \fB\-fontfile\fR (it uses a fixed \fBmonospace\fR viewer font locked to the 6x8 metric). On the raster backend \fB\-scale N\fR multiplies the pixel dimensions and the font scale by \fBN\fR.
.SS "Input grammar (Mermaid \fBpie\fR subset)"
.CS
pie                          %% header; the following are optional and in order
pie showData
pie title <text>
pie showData title <text>
title <text>                 %% alternatively on its own line
"<label>" : <value>          %% a slice; quotes optional, value int or float
%% ...                       %% comment, ignored
.CE
.PP
At least one slice is required and the values must sum to a positive number.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tupie
namespace import ::tclutils::tupie::*

set src {pie showData title Browser share
    "Chrome"  : 64
    "Safari"  : 19
    "Edge"    : 5
    "Firefox" : 3
    "Other"   : 9
}

set m [parse $src]
writePng $m chart.png -scale 3       ;# crisp raster, with legend
writeSvg $m chart.svg                ;# vector

set bytes [toPng $m -legend 0]       ;# pie only, no legend
set svg   [toSvg $m]
.CE
.PP
Through the \fBtuflow\fR facade the same source renders without an explicit model:
.CS
package require tclutils::tuflow
::tclutils::tuflow::toPng $src -scale 3      ;# facade detects the pie block
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Slice colours come from a fixed qualitative palette (10 entries) that cycles when there are more slices than colours.
.IP \(bu
A percentage label is drawn inside a slice only when the wedge is wide enough; the legend always carries label and percentage, plus the raw value when the source used \fBshowData\fR.
.IP \(bu
Labels use the \fBtupngdraw\fR 6x8 bitmap font by default, which covers ASCII and the German umlauts (real codepoints \fB\eu00xx\fR). With \fB\-fontfile\fR on the raster backend a real outline font is used via \fBfillcontours\fR (lazy \fBGlyphs\fR, unbundled); a set\-but\-missing path is a hard error, a missing \fBGlyphs\fR package degrades silently to the bitmap font.
.IP \(bu
Companion modules: \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR and \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR (backends), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (facade / dispatch), \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (the node\-edge graph renderer for the other Mermaid types).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUPIE <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no slices), \fBVALUE\fR (values do not sum to a positive number), \fBARG\fR (bad render option, e.g. non\-integer \fB\-scale\fR), \fBFONT\fR (a \fB\-fontfile\fR path that does not exist).
